        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on pilot scope, asset selection, and success criteria.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 53841,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's kick off the Cross-Plant Predictive Maintenance Rollout project. The main goal is to reduce unplanned downtime. First step is defining the pilot scope. I've started populating the Asset Criticality Matrix (A1) as per T1. My initial proposal is to focus on the CNC milling machines on Line 3 and the primary stamping press on Line 5. They have the highest impact on our production targets. Please review and share your thoughts.",
            "mentions": [
              36422,
              560411,
              18383,
              237177,
              55217
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 36422,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for kicking this off. The choice of Line 3 and 5 makes sense from an operational standpoint. Before we lock it in, can we confirm that the maintenance teams at both plants have recent experience with the sensor types we're likely to use on that press? Don't want any surprises during installation.",
            "mentions": [
              53841
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 560411,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good choices. I've checked the historical data logs, and both asset types have fairly consistent data streams, which will be great for our predictive models. This directly supports the data quality assessment risk mitigation strategy. I've added a column to A1 with a data quality score for each proposed asset.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 237177,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I can check with the garage supervisors. What kind of sensors are we talking about?",
            "mentions": [
              36422
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 55217,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I agree with the lines. Are we sure we have the budget for both? Some of that equipment is pretty old.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 36422,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Likely vibration and thermal sensors. Standard stuff, but the press housing is custom. Let's assume for now the skills are there and focus on finalizing the asset list. We can validate technician readiness as part of T8.",
            "mentions": [
              237177
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 53841,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Good point on budget. The project constraints mention limited capex. By focusing on these two high-impact assets, we're aligning with the risk mitigation plan. If there are no other major objections, I'd like to finalize this list.",
            "mentions": [
              55217
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 18383,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Sorry for the delay. The list is fine for me. I will need to check the electrical panels for space and power draw once we have the sensor specs.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 53841,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Great. Let's make that official then. DECISION: The pilot will include the CNC milling machines on Line 3 and the primary stamping press on Line 5, as detailed in A1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 36422,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Excellent. Now for success criteria. As per T7, we need to define the KPIs. I propose we track them in A6. My suggestion for the top 3 are: 1. Reduction in unplanned downtime hours, 2. Improvement in Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF), and 3. Maintenance schedule compliance.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 560411,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Those are solid outcome KPIs. I'd suggest adding a process KPI as well, like 'Time to Acknowledge Alert'. It will help us measure how quickly the teams are adopting the new workflow.",
            "mentions": [
              36422
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 55217,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "What about cost? Shouldn't we track maintenance cost savings?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 53841,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "Cost savings is a great long-term goal, but it might be hard to measure accurately within a 21-day pilot. Let's stick to operational metrics for now and add cost to the roadmap for the full rollout. I like the 'Time to Acknowledge' suggestion.",
            "mentions": [
              55217,
              560411
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 36422,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Agreed. Let's finalize the list. DECISION: The primary KPIs for the pilot are: 1. Unplanned Downtime, 2. MTBF, 3. Maintenance Compliance, and 4. Time to Acknowledge Alert. I will set up the tracking sheet A6 accordingly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 53841,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Perfect. That concludes our kickoff alignment. I will finalize the documentation for T1 by EOD.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 237177,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Ok, thanks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M17",
            "speaker_id": 18383,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Understood.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
